# Code Style

- Indent with tabs
- Single quotes for strings (double quotes only to avoid escaping)
- Omit semicolons unless required for disambiguation
- No unused variables
- Space after keywords; space before function declaration parentheses
- Always `===` / `!==`, never `==` / `!=`
- Space infix operators; space after commas
- `else` on the same line as the closing `}`
- Curly braces for multi-line `if` statements
- Always handle error parameters in callbacks
- Max line length 80 characters
- Trailing commas in multiline object/array literals

```ts
function fetchUser (id: string) {
	if (id === '') {
		throw new Error('id required')
	} else {
		return api.get(`/users/${id}`)
	}
}
```
